                "problem": "In the fork group the two 'Replication Fork' labels collide with the 'Origin' label (text merges into 'ForkOrigin' / 'OriginReplication' around x=555-600, row D/E), and the left label spills left of grid column 1 (x≈430).",
                "solution": "Line 145: self.place_in_area(fork_group, 'D1', 'F6', scale_factor=0.55) — use the full 6-column width so the bidirectional arrows span D1-D6, keep 'Origin' centered at D3/D4 and each 'Replication Fork' label at D1-D2 and D5-D6 (≥1 grid unit clearance), and shrink label text so nothing crosses left of column 1.",
                "line_number": 145,
                "object_affected": "fork_group"
            },
            {
                "problem": "The 'Topoisomerase' label (#E8623C) runs to x≈838, only ~16 px from the frame edge, and was visibly clipped while writing on; it sits in column 6 with no right margin.",
                "solution": "Line 145: self.place_at_grid(topo_label, 'C5', scale_factor=0.7) — anchor the label at C5 (right edge ≈ column 5/6 boundary) just above its orange circle at C6/D6, keeping it within 1 grid unit of the icon and fully on-screen; this area does not intersect the D1-F6 fork band.",
                "line_number": 145,
                "object_affected": "topo_label"
            },
            {
                "problem": "The helix/helicase block renders only in row B (columns 1-4), leaving rows A and C empty and a ~2-row dead gap to the fork; the yellow helicase rect + 'Helicase' label (#E8D44D) stay stranded at B4 after unzipping and never fade out.",
                "solution": "Line 83: self.place_in_area(helix, 'B1', 'C4', scale_factor=0.7) — helix occupies row B, helicase icon/label land in row C directly above the D-row fork (within 1 grid unit), and add FadeOut of the helicase label+rect once unzipping finishes so row C is clear before the fork group appears.",
                "line_number": 83,
                "object_affected": "helix"
            }
        ]
    }
